      script: `The Time Zone Room locates every passage across a grid of six zones — and let me explain the framework before we apply it. The grid has two axes: location — earth or heaven — and time — past, present, or future. That gives you six zones: earth past, earth present, earth future, heaven past, heaven present, and heaven future. Most readers only think about one zone — usually earth present, meaning "how does this apply to me today?" But every significant passage has something to say in multiple zones simultaneously, and the Time Zone Room trains you to see all six. Now watch how Philippians 2 spans the entire grid. Heaven past: "being in the form of God" — Christ existed in divine glory before anything was created. John 17:5 confirms: "the glory which I had with thee before the world was." Earth past: "was made in the likeness of men" — the incarnation in Bethlehem, a specific moment when eternity entered time and the Creator became a creature. Heaven present: Christ is exalted at the right hand of the Father — Hebrews 1:3, "sat down on the right hand of the Majesty on high." His heavenly ministry continues now, this very moment. Earth present — and this is the one that should grip you: "Let this mind be in you" is active, present tense, right now, for every believer in every century. It applies to your decision this afternoon. The argument you're having with your spouse. The grudge you're nursing at work. The pride you're protecting. Right now. Earth future: "every knee shall bow" — at the second coming and at the final judgment, the kenosis will be universally vindicated. Heaven future: "every tongue shall confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father." In the eternal state, the name above every name reigns without opposition. One passage spans eternity in both directions — and it intersects your life today.`,
