      script: `The Parallels Room reveals mirrored actions across time — and let me clarify the distinction from types, because it matters for how you study. Types are objects, offices, or events that foreshadow Christ — the Passover lamb, the temple, the brazen serpent. They point forward to fulfillment. Parallels are different: parallels are actions or events that mirror each other across different eras, revealing that God — and His adversary — work in consistent, recognizable patterns. Types deal with what things represent. Parallels deal with what beings do repeatedly. Now let me show you the most stunning parallel in all of Scripture — and this may be the single most important mirror in the Bible for understanding the Great Controversy. Isaiah 14:13-14: Lucifer said, "I will ascend into heaven. I will exalt my throne above the stars of God. I will sit also upon the mount of the congregation. I will ascend above the heights of the clouds. I will be like the Most High." Five declarations of ascent. Five grasping movements upward. And the result? "Thou shalt be brought down to hell, to the sides of the pit." He grasped and fell. Now Philippians 2:6-8: Christ, "being in the form of God, thought it not robbery to be equal with God." He had everything Lucifer craved — and did not grasp. Instead He descended. Seven steps down: emptied, servant, man, humbled, obedient, death, cross. And the result? "God hath highly exalted him and given him a name above every name." Two beings. Two opposite movements. Lucifer's five "I wills" ascended and were crushed. Christ's seven descents were crowned with glory. This parallel is the very spine of the Great Controversy: pride ascends and falls; humility descends and rises. And it's personal: every time you grasp — for control, for credit, for status — you're on Lucifer's staircase. Every time you empty — serving, forgiving, releasing — you're on Christ's. Choose your staircase.`,
